__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
app/state/
*.sqlite
*.log
.DS_Store
model-output/
data/humidity/
data/covgates/
.flubnf.env
# the Windows twin of .flubnf.env, written by setup.ps1 and called by
# FluBNF.bat: machine-specific paths, never part of the product
.flubnf.env.cmd
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
data/covidhub/

# The generated public site and its deploy workflow stay local until the lab
# decides to publish: the generator (app/core/site_build.py) is tracked, its
# output is not. A local copy lives in ~/Documents/FluBNF-local.
site/
# The site's deploy workflow is the other half of that decision, so it is
# ignored by name rather than left merely untracked, where `git add -A` would
# publish the lab's Pages deployment as a side effect of an unrelated commit.
.github/workflows/pages.yml

# Editor and agent configuration: machine-specific, never part of the product.
.claude/

# The research tree stays off the public repository for now (decision of
# 2026-08-24, taken at the v1.0.0 tag). It holds the challenger harnesses,
# their pre-registrations and their per-cell results: real evidence, but not
# a published product, and several harnesses import paths and machine
# specifics that only exist on the lab's machines. A complete copy lives in
# ~/Documents/FluBNF-local/research/, its pruned intermediates in
# ~/Documents/FluBNF-local/pruned/research/, and the evidence that never
# lived in the tree at all in ~/Documents/FluBNF-local/archive-evidence/.
# docs/RELEASE-1.0.md states this, so no ledger claim implies that the
# supporting files sit in this repository.
research/

# Manuscripts and internal analysis stay off the public repo until the lab
# decides to publish. Local copies live in ~/Documents/FluBNF-local/manuscripts.
docs/PERFORMANCE.md
docs/PARTICLE-FILTER.md
docs/figs/
